                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game shouldn't be listed under Hidden Objects tag. It is basically clicking on an item and using it to be able to get another item. It is a flash game which you can finish in less than 30 minutes without the need for any hints. The music is an awful loop, however, the locations artwork is good.\n\nThe main idea is to find a way out of the house by locating keys and items which will help you unlocking doors to find the 'ritual' room which can help you escape by opening a portal. I might have enjoyed it if it wasn't a flash game being sold on steam with a very limited soundtrack! The developer already launched many games under 'hidden objects' tag with similar gameplay! You can't lie at your customers, this is not an action game either. \n\nPros:\n+Nice artwork, not perfect but not bad. \n\nCons:\n-Bad music (One track lasts for 20 seconds before looping again and again)\n-No replay value.\n-No steam achievements.\n-Very short game (Can be finished in less than 30 minutes)\n-No steam overlay (You can't take screenshots)\n-No journal or hints to guide you if you are stuck not knowing what to do next.\n\nI won this game from steamgifts, I thought it'd be a good addition to my HOGs list, alas it doesn't even belong to that category. I always give the negatively rated games a chance, but this one proved it is not good in any way. I suggest you spend your money on another game. \n\n[quote]𝐹𝑜𝑟 𝑚𝑜𝑟𝑒 𝑟𝑒𝑣𝑖𝑒𝑤𝑠 𝑐𝘩𝑒𝑐𝑘 𝑚𝑦 𝑐𝑢𝑟𝑎𝑡𝑜𝑟 𝑝𝑎𝑔𝑒 [url=http://store.steampowered.com/curator/32399565/]𝐹𝑒𝑒𝑛𝑎'𝑠 𝐶𝘩𝑜𝑖𝑐𝑒[/url][/quote]",
